*.zip
# ...but NOT the exchange contract master. contract_size is stamped from it at capture
# and freshness.py treats it as blocking, so a 2.9 MB monthly input to STORED data
# belongs in history. The blanket *.zip rule was hiding it.
# ROOT-ANCHORED on purpose. A bare `!SecurityMaster.zip` un-ignores the name at EVERY
# level, and a second copy exists at data_agent/SecurityMaster.zip (Aug-14, 3.0 MB, newer
# than the root's Jul-30 but functionally identical: same 622 FUTSTK rows, same lots, same
# expiries — it differs only in option strikes, which nothing reads from the master).
# Every consumer reads the ROOT copy: lot_sizes.py, freshness.py, download_fundamentals.py.
# One canonical location, and the duplicate stays uncommittable.
!/SecurityMaster.zip

# Environments
*_env/
*_env_3.10/
newsindex/*_env/
newsindex/*_env_3.10/

# Sessions & states
breezesession/
zerodhasession/
.state/
.agents/

# Generated reports
newsindex/reports/

# never version these
# NOTE: git only honours '#' at the START of a line — inline comments become part
# of the pattern and silently match nothing. Keep every comment on its own line.

# abandoned PG datadir; the live cluster is /opt/homebrew/var/postgresql@18
pg_data/
# vendored MIT reference checkout (HKUDS Vibe-Trading), not our code
Vibe-Trading-main/
# working backups taken before edits
scratch/
# retired files awaiting deletion
_to_delete/
# raw Screener HTML cache — 15 MB, refetchable with
#   screener_tables.py --mode fetch
# the parsed output (screener_page_tables.csv) IS versioned; the cache is not
data_agent/fundamentals/screener_html/
_trash/
